From: dawOS <noreply@dawos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: a parameter to hand playback URBs over "as
 soon as possible"

On an xHCI host that keeps frame IDs contiguous (CFC), an isochronous
URB without URB_ISO_ASAP is given the number of the frame it starts in.
xhci_get_isoc_frame_id() wants that frame past "now + IST + 1
microframe" rounded up to a frame, and moves it one frame further when
it is the first one allowed. The samples of a playback URB are copied
when it is prepared, so they wait for the wire all that time: 2.0 to
2.5 ms on the Core Ultra 9 285K (IST: 4 microframes), measured with
usbmon on a Scarlett 18i20 4th gen (dawOS, step P1.8b).

With URB_ISO_ASAP xhci-hcd sets the SIA bit instead, and the controller
starts the URB as soon as it can.

iso_asap (default: off, nothing changes) sets the flag on the playback
data URBs. It is read when a stream is set up, so it can be written
between two runs:

  echo 1 > /sys/module/snd_usb_audio/parameters/iso_asap

This is an experiment of dawOS (step P1.8c), not a change proposed
upstream.
---
--- a/sound/usb/card.c
+++ b/sound/usb/card.c
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@
 
 bool snd_usb_use_vmalloc = true;
 bool snd_usb_skip_validation;
+bool snd_usb_iso_asap;
 
 module_param_array(index, int, NULL, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(index, "Index value for the USB audio adapter.");
@@ -107,6 +108,8 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(use_vmalloc, "Use vmalloc for PCM intermediate buffers (default: yes).");
 module_param_named(skip_validation, snd_usb_skip_validation, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(skip_validation, "Skip unit descriptor validation (default: no).");
+module_param_named(iso_asap, snd_usb_iso_asap, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(iso_asap, "Hand playback data URBs to the host controller as \"as soon as possible\" (default: no).");
 
 /* protects quirk_flags */
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(quirk_flags_mutex);
--- a/sound/usb/endpoint.c
+++ b/sound/usb/endpoint.c
@@ -1258,6 +1258,17 @@
 			goto out_of_memory;
 		u->urb->pipe = ep->pipe;
 		u->urb->transfer_flags = URB_NO_TRANSFER_DMA_MAP;
+		/*
+		 * dawOS: without URB_ISO_ASAP an xHCI host with contiguous
+		 * frame IDs gives every URB the number of the frame it starts
+		 * in, which must be a whole frame past "now + IST": the
+		 * samples, already copied, wait 2 ms and more for the wire.
+		 * With the flag the controller starts the URB as soon as it
+		 * can. Read when the stream is set up: the parameter can be
+		 * changed between two runs.
+		 */
+		if (snd_usb_iso_asap && usb_pipeout(ep->pipe))
+			u->urb->transfer_flags |= URB_ISO_ASAP;
 		u->urb->interval = 1 << ep->datainterval;
 		u->urb->context = u;
 		u->urb->complete = snd_complete_urb;
--- a/sound/usb/usbaudio.h
+++ b/sound/usb/usbaudio.h
@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@
 
 extern bool snd_usb_use_vmalloc;
 extern bool snd_usb_skip_validation;
+extern bool snd_usb_iso_asap;
 
 /*
  * Driver behavior quirk flags, stored in chip->quirk_flags
